message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PopGeneticsPro: a browser-based platform for plant population genetics with codominant, dominant, sequence and morphological data"
abstract: >-
  PopGeneticsPro is a self-contained web application for the analysis of plant population
  genetic data entirely in the browser, with no installation and no server-side computation.
  It handles codominant markers (microsatellites, SNPs, isozymes), dominant binary markers
  (AFLP, ISSR, RAPD), haploid and sequence data (chloroplast and mitochondrial alignments)
  and morphological characters within one workflow: data import from the formats of the
  classical programs, quality control, allele frequencies and diversity indices,
  Hardy-Weinberg and linkage disequilibrium tests, F-statistics and hierarchical AMOVA,
  genetic distances with ordination and trees, Bayesian clustering and assignment,
  haplotype networks and neutrality tests, demographic inference, fine-scale spatial
  genetic structure and the mating system, ending in editable publication-quality figures
  and an automatic report.
